# Keep build contexts lean and STABLE. Every image here builds from the repo
# root with `COPY . .`, and so does the race gate, so whatever is in the working
# directory is uploaded through the Docker API on every single build.
#
# The gateway repo has had this file since the start; this one did not, and it is
# the repo with the node_modules. Measured on 2026-08-28: a 1.8 GiB context, of
# which 593 MiB is node_modules, 86 MiB the panel's .next, 42 MiB .git history
# and 685 MiB a local testbed's dylaris_data. The runner is long-lived, so
# everything a job writes into the workspace stays there and is re-sent by every
# later build.
#
# Two costs, and the second is the one that hurt: the upload itself, and CACHE.
# `COPY . .` hashes the whole context, so one changed byte anywhere invalidates
# every layer after it - which is why a docs-only push recompiled every module
# under -race from scratch.
#
# None of these globs matches Go source, go.mod, go.work, or the panel sources.
.git
**/node_modules
panel/.next
node/dylaris_data
*.exe
**/*.exe
# Both patterns, because a leading-slash-free pattern here matches at the ROOT
# only - ".env*" alone caught the repo-root file and left panel/.env in the
# context. Next reads any .env it finds and INLINES NEXT_PUBLIC_* into the
# bundle at build time, so a local `docker build` produced an image with the
# developer's own API URL compiled into it. CI never saw it (fresh checkout, and
# .env is gitignored), which is exactly why it could sit here unnoticed.
.env*
**/.env*
.superpowers/

# Documentation cannot change a build or a test, so it must not invalidate one.
#
# The exceptions are not cosmetic - each is an .md the BUILD or the TESTS read,
# and each was found by looking rather than assumed:
#   core/updates/*.md      embedded into Core (core/updates/release.go), so
#                          excluding it fails loudly at go:embed
#   API.md                 core/apidoc_test.go reads it and compares it against
#                          what the generator produces
#   core/apidoc/preamble.md  the generator's input for that same comparison
# The last two run inside the race gate (go test ./... in /src/core), so leaving
# them out turns a green gate red for a reason that has nothing to do with code.
#
# Before adding another exclusion here, grep the Go and vitest sources for the
# filename. That is how these three were found.
**/*.md
!core/updates/*.md
!API.md
!core/apidoc/preamble.md
